        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Avian foraging ecology is the study of how birds acquire food efficiently under predation risk and competition. The theoretical framework — Optimal Foraging Theory (OFT) — treats foraging as an optimization problem with a defined currency (typically energy rate) and constraints (travel time, handling time, prey availability, predation risk). Birds are among the most tractable systems for testing OFT because their foraging can be observed directly, food items counted, and energetics measured."
    },
