      "text": "AERIAL FORAGERS:\n  Aerial insectivores: catch insects in flight\n    Swifts: pursue flying insects at altitude; aerial screen\n    Swallows: lower level; often near water\n    Flycatchers (tyrant + Old World): sally from perch; return\n    Distinctive: flicker response to moving prey; pursuit flight\n  Aerial plunge divers: dive from height into water\n    Gannets: 30m height, 100 km/h impact; binocular vision required\n    Kingfishers: hover + shallow dive (fresh water)\n    Terns: flutter + plunge; skim surface"
    },
