      "text": "FOLIAGE GLEANERS:\n  Probe foliage surface or interior for arthropods\n  Old World warblers (Phylloscopus): hover-glean or active search\n  Vireos: slow, methodical; large prey per item\n  Treecreepers, nuthatches: bark surface; different microhabitats\n  Resource partitioning: several species on same tree; different foraging zones\n    (MacArthur 1958: 5 warbler species on spruce trees; vertical zonation)"
