      "text": "GROUND FORAGERS:\n  Probers: bill into substrate for invertebrates\n    Godwits, curlews: tidal flat probing; tactile bill tip\n    Woodcock: earthworm detection via Herbst corpuscles in bill tip\n  Scratchers: rake ground with feet\n    Towhees, juncos, Galliformes\n  Pivoting: swing bill sideways (spoonbills; scan for fish)\n  \"Run-stop-peck\": plovers (visual; no probing)\n```"
