      "text": "VISION:\n  Tetrachromatic: UV + blue + green + red (vs trichromat humans)\n  UV vision: flowers with UV guides; plumage with UV components\n  Binocular/monocular trade-off:\n    Predators (owls, eagles): forward-facing; binocular overlap wide\n    -> depth perception for strike accuracy\n    Prey species (sparrows): lateral eyes; wide visual field; 360 near\n    -> early detection of predator\n  High density fovea: 2x human photoreceptor density\n  Temporal resolution: detect 300+ fps (useful in forest maneuver)"
    },
