      "text": "OLFACTION (stronger than assumed):\n  Procellariformes (seabirds): excellent olfaction\n    Petrels locate nest burrows and food patches by scent at sea\n  Vultures (Cathartidae, New World): detect dimethyl sulfide from decaying flesh\n    Turkey vulture (Cathartes aura): finds hidden carcasses under forest canopy\n    Old World vultures: locate carcasses visually; no olfaction\n  Kiwis: nostrils at bill tip; olfactory foraging in litter"
